  "id": "diffraction-grating",
  "term": "diffraction grating",
  "definition": "A diffraction grating is a device from which light or other radiation can be reflected so that waves of different periods are dispersed into different directions. In this way it is used to produce a spectrum, separating the radiation into distinct colour bands or lines.",
